    "text": "On 2039-11-04, the Lumina sensor array logged 18 false positives when ambient dust rose above 40 \u03bcg/m\u00b3. Cross-referencing proved that a laser calibration drift of 2.1 mm caused 12 of the false positives. The evidence does not show what caused the remaining 6 false positives.\n\nDuring the spike, internal temperatures increased from 28\u00b0C to 34\u00b0C. The evidence neither establishes the temperature increase as the cause of the remaining 6 nor excludes it.\n\nSignal reflection was ruled out as a cause.",
